WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.309 --> 00:00:10.147
<font color="#ff0000">A Netflix</font> | Original Documentary  

2
00:00:18.309 --> 00:00:22.147
A superb bird of paradise
calls for a mate.

3
00:00:26.484 --> 00:00:29.821
The pursuit of love is his life's work.

4
00:00:32.115 --> 00:00:34.993
But looking good is only half the story.

5
00:00:40.749 --> 00:00:44.711
To seal the deal,
he must charm her with his dance.

6
00:00:57.474 --> 00:00:59.726
When it comes to courting a partner,

7
00:00:59.809 --> 00:01:03.271
this superb bird of paradise
is not the only bird

8
00:01:03.396 --> 00:01:05.482
with an extraordinary display.

8
00:01:10.195 --> 00:01:11.571
But as we'll see,

9
00:01:11.863 --> 00:01:13.948
in the world of dancing birds,

10
00:01:14.324 --> 00:01:17.619
it's only the most charming that succeed.

11
00:01:58.076 --> 00:02:00.036
This is New Guinea,

12
00:02:00.120 --> 00:02:03.414
the world's largest jungle-covered island.

13
00:02:05.166 --> 00:02:07.836
In these isolated mountains and valleys,

14
00:02:07.961 --> 00:02:09.212
birds have evolved

15
00:02:09.295 --> 00:02:13.258
some of the most bizarre
courtship displays on the planet.

16
00:02:23.101 --> 00:02:26.229
Meet the King of Saxony.

17
00:02:28.606 --> 00:02:31.901
He has the longest head feathers
of any bird.

18
00:02:33.987 --> 00:02:36.656
And they're vital for impressing a female.

19
00:02:39.659 --> 00:02:43.329
But first, the king must advertise
for a queen.

20
00:02:51.337 --> 00:02:54.299
He shares the canopy
with hundreds of birds,

21
00:02:59.596 --> 00:03:02.223
but is the right one, here for him?

22
00:03:05.560 --> 00:03:07.729
Mm. That could be her.

23
00:03:08.646 --> 00:03:12.400
Time to head down to his display vine.

24
00:03:19.324 --> 00:03:21.034
She's definitely up there...

25
00:03:23.203 --> 00:03:24.954
but he needs her closer.

26
00:03:28.625 --> 00:03:30.001
And when she is,

27
00:03:30.960 --> 00:03:32.962
he can begin his routine.

28
00:03:51.397 --> 00:03:53.608
She will judge him on everything.

29
00:03:55.360 --> 00:03:57.237
How high he swings.

30
00:03:59.030 --> 00:04:01.032
The length of his head feathers.

31
00:04:03.910 --> 00:04:05.161
And how he shakes them.

32
00:04:10.208 --> 00:04:11.626
The higher he scores,

33
00:04:11.709 --> 00:04:13.753
the more likely she'll choose him.

34
00:04:28.309 --> 00:04:29.894
It's decision time.

35
00:04:34.524 --> 00:04:37.151
So, is he the king of the swings?

36
00:04:41.823 --> 00:04:43.366
It seems not.

37
00:04:46.160 --> 00:04:46.995
Oh, well,

38
00:04:47.996 --> 00:04:49.289
back to the search.

39
00:04:54.043 --> 00:04:55.962
Attracting the perfect partner

40
00:04:56.045 --> 00:04:59.048
is a challenge
for all male birds of paradise.

41
00:05:01.509 --> 00:05:03.678
So some increase their chances

42
00:05:03.761 --> 00:05:05.847
by having a permanent address.

43
00:05:12.645 --> 00:05:14.856
An old, wobbly tree stump.

44
00:05:16.399 --> 00:05:19.652
The top is just three meters
off the forest floor.

45
00:05:20.653 --> 00:05:21.988
It doesn't look much,

46
00:05:22.989 --> 00:05:24.824
but it means everything

47
00:05:24.907 --> 00:05:26.701
to this black sicklebill.

48
00:05:26.784 --> 00:05:28.661
Or SB for short.

49
00:05:32.415 --> 00:05:34.834
Every morning, SB comes here

50
00:05:34.917 --> 00:05:36.919
in the hope of attracting a female.

51
00:05:39.589 --> 00:05:41.799
And if he can't always be seen...

52
00:05:42.133 --> 00:05:44.135
he can be heard.

53
00:05:48.097 --> 00:05:52.310
Even in the dense understory,
his calls travel far.

54
00:05:54.771 --> 00:05:56.898
And, when it comes to first impressions,

55
00:05:57.190 --> 00:05:59.275
he has a neat trick up his sleeve.

56
00:06:02.695 --> 00:06:05.156
For years, no one knew why

57
00:06:05.239 --> 00:06:08.534
the black sicklebill
had these strange shoulder plumes.

58
00:06:10.411 --> 00:06:13.289
But then,
who could have imagined... this?

59
00:06:34.685 --> 00:06:37.146
With no shortage of food in these forests,

60
00:06:37.688 --> 00:06:41.025
male birds of paradise
can focus on one thing...

61
00:06:42.485 --> 00:06:45.321
attracting a mate.

62
00:06:55.456 --> 00:07:00.378
His shiny badge of feathers is a sign
that he's in tip-top condition.

63
00:07:01.421 --> 00:07:03.840
He just needs a female to spot it.

64
00:07:09.429 --> 00:07:12.181
But, with no sign of any interest,

65
00:07:12.723 --> 00:07:15.143
SB gets on with his day.

66
00:07:21.190 --> 00:07:22.066
The sicklebill

67
00:07:22.150 --> 00:07:25.528
is not the only pole-dancing bird
in these forests.

68
00:07:27.321 --> 00:07:29.657
The top of this 25-meter tree

69
00:07:29.740 --> 00:07:32.785
has been fashioned
into the perfect display post,

70
00:07:33.619 --> 00:07:37.373
by a twelve-wired bird of paradise.

71
00:07:38.583 --> 00:07:40.460
Let's call him... TW.

72
00:07:45.756 --> 00:07:48.009
From up here, TW's call

73
00:07:48.092 --> 00:07:51.596
is loud enough to carry
to the other side of the valley.

74
00:07:54.891 --> 00:07:57.435
Sadly, no one seems to be listening.

75
00:07:58.519 --> 00:08:00.313
But if a female came by,

76
00:08:00.480 --> 00:08:03.149
would she be impressed
with these moves?

77
00:08:09.906 --> 00:08:11.449
Or that tail?

78
00:08:15.411 --> 00:08:18.122
Twelve-wires
are the only birds in the world

79
00:08:18.206 --> 00:08:19.540
with a tail like this,

80
00:08:19.624 --> 00:08:23.085
and it's designed
for a very odd kind of courtship.

81
00:08:32.845 --> 00:08:35.932
He just needs a female on his pole.

82
00:08:44.732 --> 00:08:46.734
SB's post has a visitor,

83
00:08:47.318 --> 00:08:48.986
but it's a young male.

84
00:08:51.113 --> 00:08:53.074
He's not having a bad feather day,

85
00:08:53.157 --> 00:08:56.202
it's just his shoulder pads
haven't developed yet.

86
00:08:57.620 --> 00:08:59.997
And his shiny badge of feathers...

87
00:09:00.623 --> 00:09:02.500
well, they wouldn't impress anyone.

88
00:09:05.670 --> 00:09:08.673
But you're never too young
to try out your moves.

89
00:09:15.471 --> 00:09:16.639
Pretty good,

90
00:09:17.139 --> 00:09:19.100
even if he does look
like he's been dragged

91
00:09:19.183 --> 00:09:20.893
through the forest backwards.

92
00:09:26.899 --> 00:09:29.443
TW's pole has a visitor, too,

93
00:09:30.486 --> 00:09:32.613
but it's a metallic starling.

94
00:09:35.950 --> 00:09:38.327
Keen to let others know
he's in the area.

95
00:09:41.539 --> 00:09:45.876
The pole is also a great vantage point
for spying prey.

96
00:09:53.259 --> 00:09:55.177
It seems that every bird in the forest

97
00:09:55.261 --> 00:09:57.680
wants to sit on TW's post.

98
00:10:01.601 --> 00:10:03.644
But if he's ever to attract a mate,

99
00:10:03.728 --> 00:10:07.440
TW must drive off
the stream of trespassers.

100
00:10:15.740 --> 00:10:18.701
Now, where are all those
female twelve-wires?

101
00:10:20.911 --> 00:10:22.663
Surely there's one out there.

102
00:10:29.128 --> 00:10:31.422
Scruffy is still at it.

103
00:10:39.639 --> 00:10:41.766
And SB's not happy.

104
00:10:53.736 --> 00:10:55.279
The kid's got guts

105
00:10:56.781 --> 00:10:58.407
but he has to go.

106
00:10:59.784 --> 00:11:04.121
SB knows that no pole means no dates.

107
00:11:05.956 --> 00:11:07.249
Back in charge,

108
00:11:07.458 --> 00:11:08.834
it's guns out...

109
00:11:10.711 --> 00:11:11.754
hood up.

110
00:11:14.131 --> 00:11:17.259
All he needs is a passing female.

111
00:11:20.638 --> 00:11:21.639
Aha!

112
00:11:22.264 --> 00:11:23.474
Could this be the one?

113
00:11:25.643 --> 00:11:26.727
It is a female

114
00:11:26.894 --> 00:11:28.771
but not a sicklebill.

115
00:11:33.734 --> 00:11:37.321
Male birds of paradise
can go their entire lives

116
00:11:37.405 --> 00:11:39.407
without ever winning a female.

117
00:11:41.742 --> 00:11:44.036
But they're programmed to persevere.

118
00:11:50.292 --> 00:11:53.504
An approaching storm is not good news.

119
00:11:55.214 --> 00:11:58.592
SB knows there's no point
dancing in the rain.

120
00:12:04.181 --> 00:12:07.810
Female birds of paradise
never look for partners

121
00:12:08.060 --> 00:12:09.186
in bad weather.

122
00:12:15.151 --> 00:12:17.027
Or almost never.

123
00:12:17.570 --> 00:12:20.322
Here's a female
that doesn't mind the rain.

124
00:12:24.243 --> 00:12:25.828
TW can't have gone far.

125
00:12:26.829 --> 00:12:29.457
But females have little patience.

126
00:12:37.548 --> 00:12:39.967
Who knows when she'll be back.

127
00:12:42.887 --> 00:12:46.849
TW spends a lot of time
gardening and landscaping.

128
00:12:47.516 --> 00:12:50.770
It's important work
if he wants his display pole

129
00:12:50.853 --> 00:12:52.772
to stand out in the canopy.

130
00:12:58.986 --> 00:13:02.072
He's already removed
all the leaves from here.

131
00:13:09.288 --> 00:13:10.956
This lot could go, too.

132
00:13:14.668 --> 00:13:16.003
But gardening must wait.

133
00:13:16.337 --> 00:13:17.671
He has a date.

134
00:13:21.133 --> 00:13:24.553
So, will a leafy gift help to woo her?

135
00:13:30.351 --> 00:13:31.185
No.

136
00:13:35.356 --> 00:13:37.358
For a male bird of paradise,

137
00:13:37.483 --> 00:13:39.944
life can often be frustrating.

138
00:13:44.198 --> 00:13:46.450
But she hasn't given up on him yet.

139
00:13:48.285 --> 00:13:51.622
He just needs to charm her onto his pole.

140
00:14:03.133 --> 00:14:04.051
Strangely,

141
00:14:04.176 --> 00:14:08.055
female twelve-wires
like to be flicked across the face

142
00:14:08.138 --> 00:14:09.557
by a male's tail.

143
00:14:14.645 --> 00:14:16.522
And she'll judge him on this.

144
00:14:19.316 --> 00:14:20.651
So, here goes.

145
00:14:34.623 --> 00:14:38.669
Unfortunately, his technique...
is a turn-off.

146
00:14:43.549 --> 00:14:47.303
The pole dancers spend a lot of time
hoping they'll be noticed.

147
00:14:51.557 --> 00:14:54.143
But SB's wait could be over.

148
00:15:04.069 --> 00:15:06.196
That tweak is a good sign.

149
00:15:10.367 --> 00:15:13.120
But she needs a much closer inspection.

150
00:15:16.832 --> 00:15:18.834
The devil's in the detail.

151
00:15:29.637 --> 00:15:31.430
He's passed the test.

152
00:15:34.808 --> 00:15:36.894
Perseverance has paid off.

153
00:15:40.898 --> 00:15:44.610
Using a tree stump as a display post
is one thing.

154
00:15:48.948 --> 00:15:51.116
But for some dancing birds,

155
00:15:51.200 --> 00:15:53.243
the females demand even more.

156
00:15:56.372 --> 00:15:59.458
They expect their partners
to get creative.

157
00:16:07.299 --> 00:16:09.093
This is a bower.

158
00:16:09.301 --> 00:16:10.803
A stick bower.

159
00:16:12.596 --> 00:16:15.808
It's built to attract a female bowerbird.

160
00:16:17.559 --> 00:16:19.645
Though you could say it's the designer

161
00:16:19.728 --> 00:16:21.563
that really catches the eye.

162
00:16:24.650 --> 00:16:26.527
A flame bowerbird.

163
00:16:26.652 --> 00:16:29.154
The world's most brightly colored bird.

164
00:16:36.537 --> 00:16:39.039
He spent several days building his bower,

165
00:16:39.415 --> 00:16:42.418
and now he's applying
the finishing touches.

166
00:16:49.633 --> 00:16:52.886
But Flame's
is not the only kind of bower here.

167
00:17:01.311 --> 00:17:05.065
This bower is probably
the most ambitious construction

168
00:17:05.149 --> 00:17:07.568
made by any single animal.

169
00:17:20.914 --> 00:17:23.125
Here's the guy responsible.

170
00:17:24.376 --> 00:17:26.378
MacGregor's bowerbird.

171
00:17:27.671 --> 00:17:30.090
He may not have the sex appeal of Flame,

172
00:17:30.215 --> 00:17:34.970
but no other bird goes to greater heights
to impress the ladies.

173
00:17:39.266 --> 00:17:40.434
Unlike Flame,

174
00:17:40.601 --> 00:17:42.728
MacGregor spends most of the year

175
00:17:42.811 --> 00:17:44.563
tinkering with his bower.

176
00:17:50.778 --> 00:17:53.989
He works hard on making it bigger
and better.

177
00:17:57.868 --> 00:18:02.164
So far,
it's been a seven-year labor of love.

178
00:18:07.169 --> 00:18:09.922
Flame's bower,
on the other hand, is short-lived,

179
00:18:10.339 --> 00:18:12.966
likely to last just a couple of weeks.

180
00:18:14.593 --> 00:18:18.013
Even so, every stick has its place.

181
00:18:20.933 --> 00:18:23.227
And detail is everything.

182
00:18:27.940 --> 00:18:29.066
Happy with his bower,

183
00:18:29.525 --> 00:18:32.986
Flame moves his attention
to his backyard.

184
00:18:35.322 --> 00:18:39.535
If he wants to impress a female,
it's important to get this right, too.

185
00:18:42.287 --> 00:18:47.292
For both, creating the perfect
piece of art is time-consuming work.

186
00:18:49.878 --> 00:18:51.755
And occasionally frustrating.

187
00:18:55.050 --> 00:18:57.302
If only he had hands.

188
00:19:06.520 --> 00:19:08.438
This isn't MacGregor.

189
00:19:08.689 --> 00:19:11.733
It's his neighbor and rival
from along the way.

190
00:19:14.236 --> 00:19:15.362
With no one in,

191
00:19:15.696 --> 00:19:17.489
he's come to cause trouble.

192
00:19:24.121 --> 00:19:26.582
Bowerbirds can be very jealous.

193
00:19:34.631 --> 00:19:37.050
But there's a point to this vandalism.

194
00:19:38.677 --> 00:19:40.762
Sabotage your rival's bower...

195
00:19:40.888 --> 00:19:43.599
and yours may look better
to a visiting female.

196
00:19:53.192 --> 00:19:57.112
Mister Flame is still having
his own personal battles,

197
00:19:58.238 --> 00:20:00.616
but he must also watch his back.

198
00:20:02.117 --> 00:20:04.369
When you're the brightest thing
in the jungle,

199
00:20:04.453 --> 00:20:08.290
there's always a chance
you'll attract the wrong kind of bird.

200
00:20:15.255 --> 00:20:17.090
A Doria's hawk.

201
00:20:20.385 --> 00:20:22.763
But he's lost the element of surprise.

202
00:20:30.145 --> 00:20:31.521
MacGregor is back.

203
00:20:31.605 --> 00:20:33.690
And he gets on with the repairs.

204
00:20:40.197 --> 00:20:43.242
His tower is well over a meter tall.

205
00:20:45.619 --> 00:20:50.499
It may be a cliche,
but size matters to female bowerbirds.

206
00:20:53.293 --> 00:20:58.757
If a male can build and maintain
a large tower, it's a sign of good genes.

207
00:21:02.094 --> 00:21:05.305
Next, MacGregor turns his attention
to the decor.

208
00:21:08.141 --> 00:21:11.478
Every bowerbird works in his own medium.

209
00:21:13.313 --> 00:21:16.024
For MacGregor, it's sticky plant sap.

210
00:21:17.192 --> 00:21:18.652
Mm. Nice!

211
00:21:23.532 --> 00:21:26.702
Flame is decorating, too,
but he's more...

212
00:21:26.785 --> 00:21:27.744
experimental.

213
00:21:34.293 --> 00:21:37.713
MacGregor, however,
knows just what he wants.

214
00:21:42.301 --> 00:21:44.511
And everything has its place.

215
00:21:48.765 --> 00:21:51.059
Now, this has potential.

216
00:21:51.601 --> 00:21:53.353
But should it go here?

217
00:21:54.354 --> 00:21:55.188
Here?

218
00:21:57.607 --> 00:21:59.192
Or perhaps here?

219
00:21:59.651 --> 00:22:00.986
Or even here?

220
00:22:01.903 --> 00:22:02.821
Perfect.

221
00:22:07.534 --> 00:22:11.079
Fresh decorations show
that the bower is in use.

222
00:22:11.955 --> 00:22:15.625
And the fancier it is,
the more likely it'll impress a female.

223
00:22:18.670 --> 00:22:21.423
He's hung hundreds of baubles already.

224
00:22:22.257 --> 00:22:23.675
But apparently, there's a point

225
00:22:23.759 --> 00:22:26.261
when there's just one too many.

226
00:22:32.851 --> 00:22:35.270
In keeping with his brown color scheme,

227
00:22:35.354 --> 00:22:39.024
MacGregor is hoping dead flowers
will be an added attraction.

228
00:22:47.949 --> 00:22:51.036
Decor is often down to local fashion.

229
00:22:53.038 --> 00:22:55.749
In this valley, blue is the thing.

230
00:22:56.666 --> 00:22:59.127
So will these berries catch the eye?

231
00:23:06.051 --> 00:23:09.388
There's another unwelcome guest
at MacGregor's.

232
00:23:13.058 --> 00:23:14.434
This could be bad.

233
00:23:15.352 --> 00:23:19.731
But it's also an opportunity for MacGregor
to practice an important skill.

234
00:23:22.609 --> 00:23:23.485
Mimicry.

235
00:23:28.240 --> 00:23:30.450
Pretty impressive.

236
00:23:31.535 --> 00:23:34.204
And how about his squealing pig?

237
00:23:36.873 --> 00:23:39.376
He can also do... the local dogs.

238
00:23:41.670 --> 00:23:43.672
Pigs don't like dogs.

239
00:23:46.716 --> 00:23:50.303
So, what will this pig think
about a bark with more bite?

240
00:24:00.647 --> 00:24:04.443
There's more to this mimicry
than scaring pigs.

241
00:24:05.235 --> 00:24:08.280
It's also key to courting a partner.

242
00:24:15.996 --> 00:24:16.913
He's in luck.

243
00:24:16.997 --> 00:24:20.876
A female has heard him
and drops in for a closer look.

244
00:24:25.005 --> 00:24:26.882
Time for the blind audition.

245
00:24:31.470 --> 00:24:34.139
He must now give her his full repertoire.

246
00:24:37.350 --> 00:24:40.228
First up,
the songs of forest birds.

247
00:24:43.857 --> 00:24:46.109
Moving on to other sounds he's picked up

248
00:24:46.234 --> 00:24:47.486
from a nearby village.

249
00:24:49.029 --> 00:24:50.447
Like chopping wood.

250
00:24:53.241 --> 00:24:55.285
People talking.

251
00:24:58.497 --> 00:25:00.207
And, most remarkably...

252
00:25:04.044 --> 00:25:05.921
children playing!

253
00:25:13.678 --> 00:25:15.013
She's impressed.

254
00:25:15.096 --> 00:25:16.681
And who wouldn't be?

255
00:25:19.935 --> 00:25:22.020
A final dog bark...

256
00:25:22.145 --> 00:25:23.647
and it's on to stage two.

257
00:25:24.981 --> 00:25:26.691
A game of hide and seek.

258
00:25:46.753 --> 00:25:49.089
To keep her keen, he can't be seen.

259
00:26:01.434 --> 00:26:05.105
This teasing game can go on
for 20 minutes or more.

260
00:26:13.780 --> 00:26:15.865
Flame is in luck, too.

261
00:26:16.908 --> 00:26:19.619
A female flame has come to check him out.

262
00:26:24.040 --> 00:26:26.918
She replies to his call, a good sign.

263
00:26:33.675 --> 00:26:37.053
Now, how to coax her into his bower?

264
00:26:40.473 --> 00:26:44.936
Will contracting and expanding his pupil
be the right lure?

265
00:26:54.863 --> 00:26:56.406
She seems to like it.

266
00:27:00.827 --> 00:27:03.872
One more step
and she'll be in his bower.

267
00:27:23.683 --> 00:27:26.227
Oh. Too much eye work, perhaps.

268
00:27:29.939 --> 00:27:34.152
Back at MacGregor's,
it's time for the crazy thistle head.

269
00:28:10.105 --> 00:28:11.439
She's seen enough...

270
00:28:12.857 --> 00:28:14.859
but perhaps she'll be back later.

271
00:28:19.322 --> 00:28:21.741
The game's not yet up for Flame.

272
00:28:25.078 --> 00:28:26.871
His date is back.

273
00:28:28.331 --> 00:28:30.417
And he's trying something new.

274
00:28:36.339 --> 00:28:39.217
He still needs to get her into his bower,

275
00:28:40.969 --> 00:28:43.388
and a bit of blue beak bling

276
00:28:43.513 --> 00:28:45.014
might be just the thing.

277
00:28:51.146 --> 00:28:54.357
At last, she's right where he wants her.

278
00:29:04.033 --> 00:29:06.619
Time for his signature dance:

279
00:29:06.870 --> 00:29:08.246
the matador.

280
00:29:14.794 --> 00:29:18.214
Oh, dear! The pressure's getting to him.

281
00:29:23.970 --> 00:29:24.971
Take two.

282
00:29:53.291 --> 00:29:56.294
Everything seems to be going
like clockwork.

283
00:30:09.057 --> 00:30:11.017
His final move is odd.

284
00:30:11.100 --> 00:30:13.061
But it's all part of the routine.

285
00:30:23.822 --> 00:30:27.700
And this is his only contribution
to fatherhood.

286
00:30:32.372 --> 00:30:35.583
Bowerbirds play the mating game alone.

287
00:30:38.711 --> 00:30:41.756
But in the jungles of Central
and South America,

288
00:30:42.215 --> 00:30:45.552
there are some birds
whose only hope of finding love

289
00:30:45.677 --> 00:30:47.053
is teamwork.

290
00:30:55.937 --> 00:30:58.690
This is a Guianan cock-of-the-rock.

291
00:31:01.943 --> 00:31:06.990
Every morning, a posse of males
gathers in this patch of forest

292
00:31:07.240 --> 00:31:09.826
in the hope of some female action.

293
00:31:21.004 --> 00:31:24.883
They're not exactly friends
but they need one another to succeed.

294
00:31:29.262 --> 00:31:32.599
So, chaos must give way to order.

295
00:31:39.063 --> 00:31:41.399
This is a communal display ground,

296
00:31:41.691 --> 00:31:42.734
or lek.

297
00:31:49.782 --> 00:31:50.742
At the lek,

298
00:31:50.909 --> 00:31:53.578
every male has his own dancing area.

299
00:31:55.705 --> 00:31:57.332
And the more males there are,

300
00:31:57.790 --> 00:32:00.043
the more likely females will visit.

301
00:32:06.341 --> 00:32:10.470
Teamwork is even more important
for some performers in Panama.

302
00:32:12.972 --> 00:32:14.766
This is the dancing perch

303
00:32:14.849 --> 00:32:17.560
of a male lance-tailed manakin.

304
00:32:18.937 --> 00:32:20.355
But to attract a female,

305
00:32:20.438 --> 00:32:22.565
one manakin just won't cut it.

306
00:32:23.691 --> 00:32:25.985
So... he has a wingman.

307
00:32:31.658 --> 00:32:35.411
The manakins here
are part of a 21-year study,

308
00:32:35.578 --> 00:32:39.123
and this pair has worked together
for five years.

309
00:32:48.341 --> 00:32:50.176
They're a well-oiled machine.

310
00:32:52.929 --> 00:32:55.848
And the most successful duo
in this forest.

311
00:33:01.729 --> 00:33:02.814
Rehearsal over,

312
00:33:03.064 --> 00:33:05.066
the pair go in search of a mate.

313
00:33:07.694 --> 00:33:10.154
They advertise their readiness
with a duet.

314
00:33:15.827 --> 00:33:18.287
And their calls have been answered.

315
00:33:19.956 --> 00:33:24.460
Now, they show her their stage
with a round of flybys.

316
00:33:40.643 --> 00:33:42.353
So far, so good.

317
00:33:46.107 --> 00:33:48.568
But will their routine hit the mark?

318
00:33:56.784 --> 00:33:59.746
If it does, only the alpha will mate.

319
00:34:01.289 --> 00:34:02.874
The wingman's only here

320
00:34:02.957 --> 00:34:04.917
to make his boss look good.

321
00:34:11.799 --> 00:34:13.176
But, before deciding,

322
00:34:13.259 --> 00:34:17.138
female manakins always check out
the competition.

323
00:34:19.057 --> 00:34:20.391
Oh, shame!

324
00:34:23.603 --> 00:34:25.396
At the cock-of-the-rock lek,

325
00:34:25.480 --> 00:34:27.899
the judges are taking their seats.

326
00:34:31.611 --> 00:34:34.238
It's got the posse excited again.

327
00:34:47.335 --> 00:34:50.880
Order restored, each takes his position.

328
00:34:54.509 --> 00:34:56.844
And presents his best side.

329
00:35:02.350 --> 00:35:04.977
They'll be judged on their rear ends.

330
00:35:15.571 --> 00:35:19.325
It takes a trained eye
to spot the prettiest bottom.

331
00:35:22.411 --> 00:35:24.622
But there's more to the contest
than that.

332
00:35:29.001 --> 00:35:30.294
Wait for it...

333
00:35:41.597 --> 00:35:43.933
Yeah, okay, it's not exactly Swan Lake,

334
00:35:44.016 --> 00:35:46.727
but it's enough to make
the final choice easier.

335
00:35:58.406 --> 00:36:01.993
But is this male as impressive...
up close?

336
00:36:08.749 --> 00:36:11.544
He must keep hopping
until he gets the okay.

337
00:36:15.882 --> 00:36:18.467
Not everyone's best pleased about that.

338
00:36:21.262 --> 00:36:23.931
But the competition isn't over yet.

339
00:36:28.144 --> 00:36:31.063
There are still other females
to win over,

340
00:36:32.773 --> 00:36:34.025
so they must keep hopping.

341
00:36:46.162 --> 00:36:48.748
But when the next female chooses...

342
00:36:50.583 --> 00:36:52.293
it's the same guy!

343
00:36:54.003 --> 00:36:56.339
Research has shown that most matings

344
00:36:56.422 --> 00:36:58.716
at a lek are with one male.

345
00:37:02.053 --> 00:37:03.596
But only the females know

346
00:37:03.679 --> 00:37:06.349
what he has that the others don't.

347
00:37:10.102 --> 00:37:13.856
Still, until the last female's gone,
there's always hope.

348
00:37:24.450 --> 00:37:27.328
The manakin A-team are hopeful, too.

349
00:37:29.330 --> 00:37:31.165
The female's back.

350
00:37:34.377 --> 00:37:36.337
And the duo picks up where they left off.

351
00:37:52.645 --> 00:37:55.106
But the final act... is a solo.

352
00:37:57.233 --> 00:37:59.527
So, when it's time to go it alone,

353
00:37:59.610 --> 00:38:02.571
the alpha calls at his wingman to leave.

354
00:38:08.828 --> 00:38:13.040
Last year, this male
was the most successful in the study.

355
00:38:15.459 --> 00:38:17.461
But he can't afford to relax.

356
00:38:20.381 --> 00:38:23.509
Research has shown that older females,
like this one,

357
00:38:23.592 --> 00:38:27.555
make experienced males work harder
for their affections.

358
00:38:30.349 --> 00:38:33.978
So he must dazzle her
with each of his dance moves.

359
00:38:40.568 --> 00:38:43.696
Now comes the highlight
of the whole performance.

360
00:38:45.323 --> 00:38:46.615
Cue drumroll...

361
00:38:52.163 --> 00:38:53.664
The perch bounces.

362
00:39:04.800 --> 00:39:06.177
She likes them!

363
00:39:10.890 --> 00:39:12.850
All that's left is to bow...

364
00:39:12.933 --> 00:39:13.893
and mate.

365
00:39:16.228 --> 00:39:18.356
The wingman can only look on.

366
00:39:18.439 --> 00:39:20.900
Perhaps next year, he'll be on top.

367
00:39:28.449 --> 00:39:29.992
Back in New Guinea,

368
00:39:30.368 --> 00:39:33.913
there's one dancing bird
that has it all...

369
00:39:36.665 --> 00:39:38.042
the perfect arena,

370
00:39:38.501 --> 00:39:40.503
the most varied dance routine,

371
00:39:40.711 --> 00:39:42.797
and he does it all by himself.

372
00:39:44.090 --> 00:39:47.510
You could say...
he's the greatest showman.

373
00:39:52.056 --> 00:39:55.059
This is his personal display court.

374
00:39:56.519 --> 00:39:57.937
He's a bird of paradise,

375
00:39:58.354 --> 00:40:00.564
a Carola's parotia,

376
00:40:01.607 --> 00:40:03.317
and his name's Bob.

377
00:40:07.530 --> 00:40:10.574
Bob is obsessed with tidiness.

378
00:40:11.617 --> 00:40:13.077
But it's vital housework.

379
00:40:16.497 --> 00:40:20.292
Female Carolas
don't visit messy display courts.

380
00:40:23.087 --> 00:40:25.047
Every leaf must go.

381
00:40:29.135 --> 00:40:29.969
Perfect.

382
00:40:32.346 --> 00:40:34.640
But Bob's jobs are not done.

383
00:40:36.517 --> 00:40:38.436
There's other groundwork to do.

384
00:40:43.607 --> 00:40:46.277
His arena is carpeted with moss.

385
00:40:46.944 --> 00:40:49.321
And there are a few areas to attend to.

386
00:40:56.579 --> 00:40:57.621
Splendid!

387
00:40:59.999 --> 00:41:02.751
Chores finished, Bob limbers up.

388
00:41:05.421 --> 00:41:08.716
Carolas spend more time
rehearsing their displays

389
00:41:08.841 --> 00:41:10.801
than any other bird of paradise.

390
00:41:18.184 --> 00:41:23.147
The ballerina is just one
of nine carefully choreographed moves.

391
00:41:24.899 --> 00:41:28.694
And each will have to be done
in exactly the right order,

392
00:41:30.613 --> 00:41:34.366
making it the most complex dance
of any bird.

393
00:41:38.245 --> 00:41:42.249
Even the pauses between moves
are important to the routine.

394
00:41:44.627 --> 00:41:47.963
And it's not just what he does but where.

395
00:41:49.089 --> 00:41:51.634
Dancing under his perch is crucial,

396
00:41:51.717 --> 00:41:55.471
as it's from here
a female will view his performance.

397
00:42:03.896 --> 00:42:07.691
But even the most serious dancer
can tire of practicing.

398
00:42:07.775 --> 00:42:10.611
Particularly when no one's even watching.

399
00:42:13.447 --> 00:42:15.616
So, it's off to lunch.

400
00:42:19.745 --> 00:42:20.996
With Bob gone,

401
00:42:21.288 --> 00:42:22.665
others slide in.

402
00:42:25.501 --> 00:42:26.835
A juvenile male

403
00:42:26.919 --> 00:42:29.797
and his equally juvenile male friend.

404
00:42:31.715 --> 00:42:34.260
One day,
they'll both have their own courts

405
00:42:34.343 --> 00:42:38.097
but until then, they must seize
every chance to practice.

406
00:42:41.809 --> 00:42:44.228
With two, they can role-play.

407
00:42:47.356 --> 00:42:48.274
A dancer...

408
00:42:49.942 --> 00:42:51.527
and a judging female.

409
00:42:59.410 --> 00:43:00.536
But time's up.

410
00:43:02.913 --> 00:43:04.039
Bob's back.

411
00:43:08.669 --> 00:43:11.046
This youngster wants to stick around

412
00:43:11.130 --> 00:43:12.423
and learn from an expert.

413
00:43:17.928 --> 00:43:19.805
But playtime is over.

414
00:43:22.516 --> 00:43:24.518
And not a moment too soon.

415
00:43:26.437 --> 00:43:28.022
A female Carola.

416
00:43:31.609 --> 00:43:33.527
But she's not looking for love.

417
00:43:34.778 --> 00:43:36.780
She's after nest material.

418
00:43:39.742 --> 00:43:41.076
Best get rid of her.

419
00:43:47.750 --> 00:43:50.085
When you're a Carola's parotia,

420
00:43:50.336 --> 00:43:52.630
there's no such thing as downtime.

421
00:43:56.592 --> 00:44:00.888
To succeed,
Bob knows his routine must be faultless.

422
00:44:03.641 --> 00:44:07.061
So it's practice, practice, practice.

423
00:44:12.608 --> 00:44:14.985
Aha! Another female!

424
00:44:17.821 --> 00:44:19.948
This one seems interested in him,

425
00:44:20.157 --> 00:44:22.117
so it's showtime.

426
00:44:25.371 --> 00:44:27.623
Bob opens with a perch pivot,

427
00:44:28.248 --> 00:44:30.209
the first of his nine moves.

428
00:44:43.847 --> 00:44:47.393
With the female getting closer,
it's time for move two.

429
00:44:48.560 --> 00:44:49.853
The court hops.

430
00:44:51.355 --> 00:44:53.482
Then smartly onto move three,

431
00:44:53.899 --> 00:44:55.609
the swaying bounce.

432
00:44:58.237 --> 00:45:02.116
The mossy carpet helps keep Bob's feet
firmly on the ground.

433
00:45:03.575 --> 00:45:06.161
But he needs her on his perch.

434
00:45:10.207 --> 00:45:11.041
Yes!

435
00:45:13.502 --> 00:45:14.461
But what's this?

436
00:45:14.586 --> 00:45:15.796
A plus-one?

437
00:45:17.381 --> 00:45:20.134
It's another adult male.

438
00:45:22.803 --> 00:45:25.806
He could prove trouble
but Bob must press on.

439
00:45:29.268 --> 00:45:32.312
A Carola display could last hours.

440
00:45:33.647 --> 00:45:35.149
And there are points for stamina.

441
00:45:43.157 --> 00:45:46.368
The arrival of a second male
is more worrying.

442
00:45:50.831 --> 00:45:53.667
Suddenly, Bob's surrounded by rivals,

443
00:45:53.792 --> 00:45:55.586
here to break up his date.

444
00:45:56.253 --> 00:46:00.299
If he loses focus now,
she may visit one of their courts instead.

445
00:46:01.800 --> 00:46:04.094
And he's still got a lot to get through.

446
00:46:06.138 --> 00:46:07.389
Next, move four.

447
00:46:08.265 --> 00:46:09.558
The head tilts.

448
00:46:16.190 --> 00:46:19.276
But all that noise
is just too distracting.

449
00:46:24.198 --> 00:46:26.408
He must show them who's boss.

450
00:46:28.827 --> 00:46:31.789
And this bit of leaf could be the answer.

451
00:46:33.957 --> 00:46:37.336
It's a badge of ownership,
a Carola's way of saying:

452
00:46:37.419 --> 00:46:39.963
"This is my court. Get lost."

453
00:46:47.221 --> 00:46:48.096
It's odd...

454
00:46:50.307 --> 00:46:51.433
but it works.

455
00:46:56.939 --> 00:46:58.899
But now, something's wrong.

456
00:47:01.109 --> 00:47:02.736
Has she lost interest,

457
00:47:02.903 --> 00:47:06.448
or is he trying to woo her
at the wrong end of the perch?

458
00:47:12.162 --> 00:47:13.038
Fortunately,

459
00:47:13.121 --> 00:47:15.541
Bob's remembered that female Carolas

460
00:47:15.624 --> 00:47:18.877
like to look down
on their would-be partners.

461
00:47:21.004 --> 00:47:25.259
So it's back to business,
and the second round of court hops.

462
00:47:25.342 --> 00:47:26.426
Move five.

463
00:47:35.727 --> 00:47:37.521
Now on to the next move:

464
00:47:37.604 --> 00:47:39.022
the hop and shake.

465
00:47:39.231 --> 00:47:40.190
Number six,

466
00:47:40.607 --> 00:47:43.527
where he'll fluff his feathers,
shuffle forward,

467
00:47:44.194 --> 00:47:45.696
and stick his head under his wing.

468
00:47:48.782 --> 00:47:51.577
Fluff, shuffle, wing.

469
00:47:52.703 --> 00:47:53.662
Fluff...

470
00:47:53.787 --> 00:47:54.746
shuffle...

471
00:47:54.955 --> 00:47:55.789
wing.

472
00:47:57.374 --> 00:47:59.042
Still looking good above.

473
00:48:02.546 --> 00:48:05.966
So it's time for moves seven,
eight and nine.

474
00:48:06.049 --> 00:48:08.760
The bow, ballerina and head bobs,

475
00:48:09.678 --> 00:48:13.891
the moves that mark him out
as surely the finest dancer of them all.

476
00:48:17.936 --> 00:48:19.479
Take it away, Bob!

477
00:48:22.441 --> 00:48:25.444
♪ I was dancing when I was twelve ♪

478
00:48:28.864 --> 00:48:32.200
♪ I was dancing when I was twelve ♪

479
00:48:35.203 --> 00:48:38.707
♪ I was dancing when I was out ♪

480
00:48:41.585 --> 00:48:44.796
♪ I was dancing when I was out ♪

481
00:48:47.841 --> 00:48:50.761
♪ I danced myself out of the womb ♪

482
00:48:53.805 --> 00:48:56.141
♪ I danced myself out of the womb ♪

483
00:48:56.224 --> 00:48:59.686
Some male Carolas never win
the female...

484
00:49:00.103 --> 00:49:03.148
♪ Is it strange to dance that soon? ♪

485
00:49:03.398 --> 00:49:05.692
but Bob's chances are looking good.

486
00:49:06.026 --> 00:49:09.112
♪ I danced myself out of the womb ♪

487
00:49:11.615 --> 00:49:14.326
♪ Ohh ♪

488
00:49:14.785 --> 00:49:17.245
♪ Ohh-oh-ohh ♪

489
00:49:18.538 --> 00:49:21.833
♪ I was dancing when I was eight ♪

490
00:49:24.795 --> 00:49:27.297
♪ I was dancing when I was eight ♪

491
00:49:27.673 --> 00:49:30.884
Even the pauses are holding her interest.

492
00:49:30.968 --> 00:49:34.388
♪ Is it strange to dance so late? ♪

493
00:49:37.099 --> 00:49:40.394
♪ Is it strange to dance so late? ♪

494
00:49:42.479 --> 00:49:45.440
♪ Ohh ♪

495
00:49:45.524 --> 00:49:47.776
♪ Ohh-oh-ohh ♪

496
00:50:03.041 --> 00:50:06.628
Fluttering wings
are her way of saying:

497
00:50:06.712 --> 00:50:08.088
"Nice job, Bob."

498
00:50:10.716 --> 00:50:13.176
It's the sign he's been hoping for.

499
00:50:19.224 --> 00:50:20.392
Hurrah!

500
00:50:23.353 --> 00:50:26.523
But despite Bob's virtuoso performance...

501
00:50:26.648 --> 00:50:28.984
she may never want to see him again.

502
00:50:32.195 --> 00:50:33.030
Oh, well.

503
00:50:34.195 --> 00:50:45.030
Subtitles: Perfect
